      "reviews": "“It’s probably the first horror game I’ve encountered where it’s obvious that no detail was left untouched. This game isn’t just about scaring you; it’s about making you feel helpless and vulnerable while playing on your childhood fears.”<br>The Outerhaven<br><br>“The grainy black-and-white horror film aesthetic is a real treat, building dread and tension rather than relying on gore to terrify.”<br>Cliqist<br><br>“Developed and published by Coven Games, Witchkin seems to have been birthed from hell itself. Set to haunt your dreams mid-2017, Witchkin is definitely a game you’ll want to play with friends...”<br>Gamer Assault Weekly<br>",
